# Rust build output
/target/

# cargo-mutants writes its working copy and its report here on every `just
# mutants` run, in the repo root. Phase 3 is where that target starts being
# used, so the entry lands before the first run that would leave it untracked.
/mutants.out/
/mutants.out.old/

# Upstream library docs pulled in for reading (kube-rs, ratatui, k8s).
# Never committed — CLAUDE.md § Source files.
/tmp/

# Key material, in case a generator is killed between writing a key and its
# own cleanup trap — `kill -9` does not run the trap, and `git add -A` does not
# ask. scripts/make-certs.sh writes here; the certificates it keeps are
# *.crt.pem, which stay committed.
*.key.pem
*.key
kubeconfig*.yaml

__pycache__/

# Agent scratch
/.agent/
# The session handoff note — where the last turn stopped and what the next one
# picks up. Written in Turkish, which no committed file may be (CLAUDE.md §
# Language), and true only until the next session reads it. Ignored so
# `git add -A` cannot sweep it in.
/last.md
.claude/settings.local.json
# .claude/agents/ is deliberately NOT ignored: the five subagent definitions
# are part of how this project is built (CLAUDE.md § Agent workflow), and a
# clone without them cannot follow that section.

# Editors
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~

# Core dumps. A killed process drops `core.<pid>` in the working directory, and
# `git add -A` does not ask: an operator review's stray `pkill` left 16 of them,
# 149 MB, in the repo root on 2026-08-22. The name is the kernel's default
# `core_pattern` and a tuned one still starts with it.
core.*
core

# OS
.DS_Store
